{% block title %}Wi-Fi access point lost power or connection from its switch{% endblock %}
{% block crew %}
{% if confirmed %}
Wi-Fi is not working in {{ where }}{% if services %} ({{ services | join_and }}){% endif %}: the Wi-Fi unit there has lost power from the network cabinet. The ETO should check the network cabinet that feeds it.
{% else %}
Wi-Fi is probably not working in {{ where }}{% if services %} ({{ services | join_and }}){% endif %}: the Wi-Fi unit there seems to have lost its connection to the network cabinet. The ETO should check the network cabinet that feeds it.
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block summary %}{{ device }} on {{ switch }} port {{ port }}: link {{ "down" if link_up is false else "up" }}{% if poe_w is not none %}, PoE {{ poe_w }} W{% else %}, PoE power data not available{% endif %}; the access point is not answering.{% endblock %}
{% block causes %}
- PoE disabled or the switch's PoE budget exceeded
- Cable or patch fault between the switch and the access point
- Switch reboot or power event
{% endblock %}
{% block steps %}
- Check {{ switch }} port {{ port }}: PoE mode, power draw and link
- Check the switch's PoE budget
- Check the patch cable and the access point's connection
{% endblock %}
{% block engineer %}Attachment from {{ attachment }}.{% endblock %}
